// endpoint_set_session_model.proto — SetSessionModel: change the model for every response
// from the NEXT turn on.
//
// RESOLVES AFTER THE CURRENT TURN ENDS, never mid-turn: the switch takes
// effect between turns, so a turn is answered by one model throughout, and
// this call returns only once that boundary has passed. With no turn open it
// resolves at once.
//
// A MODEL SWITCH IS A COLD CACHE. The prompt cache is per model, so the next
// request re-reads the whole context whatever the TTL. The same discipline as
// StartSession applies: the request names the size above which that cost is
// NOT to be paid unasked; a larger context is refused IMMEDIATELY — before
// any waiting — with the cost, and the daemon retries naming a remediation.

